{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_device_list_tree_sortable_design", "label": "Device-List Parent/Child + Sortable Subnet List Design (F3)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-netis-device-list-tree-sortable-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_device_list_tree_sortable_design_device_table", "label": "Shared Sortable deviceTable (base-path links)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-netis-device-list-tree-sortable-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both features hinge on one refactor: extract the sortable table into a reusable component whose sort links take a base path, so it renders on both /devices and /subnets/{id} with sort links staying on the hosting page."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_device_list_tree_sortable_design_group_by_parent", "label": "GroupByParent Tree Grouping", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-netis-device-list-tree-sortable-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stable DFS preserving the applied sort within sibling sets; an orphan whose parent is filtered out is treated as a root so no row is ever dropped; a visited set guards cyclic parent references guaranteeing termination. Only the Devices page is grouped \u2014 the subnet list is a filtered subset where the parent is often absent, so it stays flat; grid tiles stay flat as a spatial overview."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_device_list_tree_sortable_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_12_netis_device_list_tree_sortable_design_device_table", "relation": "references", "confide